# Solventa Gradle

These rules live with the Android app and apply only to Gradle files under `apps/mobile/`. Do not use them for `apps/web/` or `apps/backend/`.

The mobile client is its own Gradle build. Do not share a build tool with the Angular web app or the Python services.

- Declare dependency versions only in `apps/mobile/Solventa/gradle/libs.versions.toml`.
- Reference them with `alias(libs.plugins...)` and `libs.*`. Do not hardcode versions in module scripts.
- `minSdk` is 24. `compileSdk` and `targetSdk` are 37. JVM target is 11.
- `applicationId` and `namespace` stay `com.grupo8_uniandes.solventa`.

```kotlin
plugins {
    alias(libs.plugins.android.application)
    alias(libs.plugins.kotlin.compose)
}

dependencies {
    implementation(libs.androidx.compose.material3)
}
```
